  "body_html": "<h1>Extensive Game With Imperfect Information</h1>\n<p>An extensive game with imperfect information keeps the tree, player assignments,\nand terminal payoffs of an extensive form, but also records what each player knows\nwhen making a move. This is represented by information sets that group decision\nnodes a player cannot distinguish.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 6.3] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MechDesign.pdf</code>. Imperfect information extends the extensive form model by adding information sets.</li>\n</ul>",
